        "# **COMP 5600/6600 Final Project :- Story-to-Algorithms: Building a Narrative Equity Model Using BERT-Based Sentiment Analysis**\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Name:** Princess Chihurumnaya Samuel\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Abstract:**\n",
        "\n",
        "Marginalization and microaggressions embedded in textual narratives contribute to systemic inequities, often missed by traditional sentiment analysis. This project, \"Story-to-Algorithms,\" introduces a BERT-based model to classify narratives for harmful content, transforming subjective stories into actionable insights for equity auditing. Using the Social Bias Inference Corpus (SBIC.v2), a dataset of ~150,000 social media posts, we fine-tuned a BERT-base-uncased model for binary classification (harmful vs. benign), aggregating labels with a 0.5 offensiveness score threshold. A dataset size ablation study (1,000 to 35,933 examples) revealed performance scaling, with accuracy rising from 75.5% to 84.6% and macro F1 from 74.5% to 84.1%. An optimal training threshold was observed around 10,000 examples. The framework includes an inference pipeline and an interactive UI for real-time analysis. This work contributes to equitable NLP by bridging narrative equity with algorithmic bias detection, mitigating biases in AI-driven content moderation.\n",
        "\n",
        "(**NOTE:** Full discussion of this projects' implementation and results can be found in my mid-project report, final-project report, and also presentation submissions)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UNAIeVhh4tm2"
      }
    },
