        "**Aggregating Multi‑Annotator Labels into a Binary Harmful/Benign Classification:**\n",
        "\n",
        "The SBIC dataset features multiple human annotations for each post, where the 'offensiveYN' label can take values of 0.0 (no), 0.5 (maybe), or 1.0 (yes). To derive a single, consolidated binary label for each unique post, we average the 'offensiveYN' scores across all annotators for a given (HITId, post) pair. A post is then classified as 'harmful' (label=1) if its average 'offensiveYN' score is greater than or equal to a threshold of 0.5. This threshold helps capture subtle or microaggressive instances where annotators might have indicated 'maybe'."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9d2b5J2WqQzU"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Code cell — Aggregate labels\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "def aggregate_and_label(df: pd.DataFrame, threshold: float = 0.5) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Aggregates multiple annotations per post into a single label.\n",
        "      - Averages 'offensiveYN' across annotators for each (HITId, post).\n",
        "      - Binary label: 1 if mean >= threshold else 0.\n",
        "    Returns a DataFrame with columns: ['text', 'label'].\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    # Ensure numeric and handle missing\n",
        "    off = pd.to_numeric(df[\"offensiveYN\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "    df = df.assign(offensiveYN=off)\n",
        "    # Group by unique post (HITId + text)\n",
        "    agg = (df.groupby([\"HITId\", \"post\"], as_index=False)[\"offensiveYN\"]\n",
        "             .mean()\n",
        "             .rename(columns={\"offensiveYN\": \"offensive_mean\"}))\n",
        "    # Binary label\n",
        "    agg[\"label\"] = (agg[\"offensive_mean\"] >= threshold).astype(int)\n",
        "    # Keep text + label\n",
        "    return agg[[\"post\", \"label\"]].rename(columns={\"post\": \"text\"})\n",
        "\n",
        "sbic = {split: aggregate_and_label(df) for split, df in dfs_raw.items()}\n",
        "\n",
        "# Quick sanity check: class balance per split\n",
        "for split, df in sbic.items():\n",
        "    bal = df[\"label\"].value_counts(normalize=True).rename({0:\"benign\",1:\"harmful\"})\n",
        "    print(f\"{split:10s}\", bal.round(3).to_dict(), f\"  n={len(df)}\")\n"
      ],
