        "**Fine‑tuning BERT and Sweeping Training Set Sizes:**\n",
        "\n",
        "This section conducts an experiment to understand the impact of training data size on model performance. We fine-tune the bert-base-uncased model (or distilbert-base-uncased) for a few epochs across different subsets of the training data, starting from 1,000 examples up to the full training set. For each training run, we evaluate the model's performance on the fixed test set. We track two key metrics: Accuracy and Macro-F1 score, with Macro-F1 being particularly important due to potential class imbalance in the 'harmful' vs. 'benign' labels. The results will demonstrate how performance scales with increased training data."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TbJII1v_quly"
      }
