        "**Gradio Web Application (Shareable UI):**\n",
        "\n",
        "This cell offers an alternative, more shareable user interface using the gradio library. Unlike ipywidgets which are confined to the notebook, Gradio generates a browser-based UI that can be easily shared via a public link. It provides a text input box and displays the model's predictions and class probabilities in a clear, interactive format. I included this as I considered it ideal for quickly demonstrating the model in the presentation I submitted."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VN8BBPcprbbs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Code cell — Gradio app (Shareable UI)\n",
        "# -------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "# !pip install -q gradio\n",
        "\n",
        "import gradio as gr\n",
        "\n",
        "def predict_ui(txt: str):\n",
        "    txt = txt or \"\"\n",
        "    label, probs = classify_text(txt)\n",
        "    return (\n",
        "        f\"{label.upper()}\",\n",
        "        {\"benign\": probs[\"benign\"], \"harmful\": probs[\"harmful\"]}\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "theme = gr.themes.Soft(\n",
        "    primary_hue=\"orange\",\n",
        "    secondary_hue=\"slate\"\n",
        ").set(\n",
        "    body_background_fill=LIGHT_GREY,\n",
        "    body_text_color=AUBURN_BLUE\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "demo = gr.Interface(\n",
        "    fn=predict_ui,\n",
        "    inputs=gr.Textbox(lines=6, placeholder=\"Type or paste text here...\", label=\"Enter text\"),\n",
        "    outputs=[gr.Textbox(label=\"Prediction\"), gr.Label(num_top_classes=2, label=\"Class probabilities\")],\n",
        "    title=\"Microaggressions / Marginalization Detector (BERT)\",\n",
        "    description=(\"Research demo. Content warning: user text may include harmful language. \"\n",
        "                 \"Predictions are probabilistic and can be wrong.\"),\n",
        "    theme=theme,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set share=True if you want a public link (beware of security/abuse).\n",
        "# demo.launch(share=True)\n",
        "# For local:\n",
        "demo.launch()"
